Embed a saved public @@NAME@@ ticket form with a block or shortcode. Manage your event and orders in the external service.

== Description ==

This is a frontend integration with the @@MARKET@@ @@NAME@@ service. You need an organizer account and a saved, published form in that service. The plugin provides one Gutenberg block, one shortcode and local onboarding under Settings > @@NAME@@. No WooCommerce or API keys are required. The plugin is free. The external service has its own organizer pricing and terms; see @@OFFER_URL@@ for its current offer. WordPress does not process service fees.

Create and save a form in @@NAME@@. Copy its public URL, then insert the @@NAME@@ block and paste the URL. Publish the page. Use only @@ORIGIN@@/form/saved-slug, without query parameters or fragments. The editor shows local controls, never a remote administration screen.

Shortcode:
[@@SHORTCODE@@ url="@@ORIGIN@@/form/saved-slug" title="Tickets for our event"]

Fixed height:
[@@SHORTCODE@@ url="@@ORIGIN@@/form/saved-slug" mode="fixed" height="800"]

Website appearance (optional):
[@@SHORTCODE@@ url="@@ORIGIN@@/form/saved-slug" inherit_style="true"]

"Match website style" is enabled by default. Disable it in the block or set inherit_style="false" to keep the service appearance. It uses the surrounding website font family and colors. Custom font-face URLs are passed to the form; their servers must allow cross-origin font loading. Unreadable stylesheets or blocked fonts retain the supplied font-family fallback. The seat map keeps the service appearance. This option requires /embed.js even with fixed height.

Height is limited to 240-4000 pixels. Automatic mode uses the existing service helper. A standalone form link remains available without the helper. Multiple forms can appear on one page. Event settings, inventory, order processing, payments, ticket delivery and admission remain owned by @@NAME@@. The plugin does not implement any payment gateway. Embedded payment methods and browser compatibility require verification for the particular event; card gateways and bank-app handoffs are not guaranteed.

= External service and privacy =

On a published page with a configured form, the visitor's browser connects to @@ORIGIN@@ to load /form/<saved-slug>?embed=1. Automatic height or website appearance also loads @@ORIGIN@@/embed.js once per page. This connection shares the visitor's IP address, browser information and any referrer allowed by the site's policy. The visitor enters purchase data directly into the service iframe. The helper exchanges resize/viewport/scroll, optional bounded presentation/font settings and displayed ticket counts/prices with the form. Customer contact details, order identifiers, payment instructions, authentication secrets and order submissions are not passed to WordPress.

The service may use its configured backend, assets, storage and payment providers. Review its privacy information and the needs of your own website before publishing; this plugin does not claim that the service is cookie-free. The WordPress plugin does not add analytics or tracking pixels. The external service has its own privacy practices, described in its privacy policy. Optional website appearance loads the website font URLs inside the service iframe. Activation, local help and editing do not fetch the remote form. WordPress stores the public URL and presentation attributes, not customer orders, organizer passwords or service API keys. No server-side HTTP request is made by the plugin.

